WEBVTT

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.730
Though one may gaze skyward from the very same place,

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.810
they will never see the same clouds twice.

00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:18.500
The days of our lives leave their mark on the march of time.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:22.720
Woo-hoo! I won tickets to the screening!

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:23.940
Hooray!

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.710
Oh god, I sound just like Arashiyama.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.870
Is she starting to rub off on me?

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.560
Uh-oh, I better be careful.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.970
Well anyway, I've cleared the first step!

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.010
Now to get Sanada to come with me!

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:25.080
Hey, what's that?

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:26.900
I wanna go! I wanna go!

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.640
It's the final showdown of the evil syndicates!

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.360
Sorry, but I'm gonna go with Sanada-kun.

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:36.460
But whenever I try to ask him, I chicken out!

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:39.550
Oh, how very bittersweet. Yes, Haribara-san?

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:42.590
'Tis the joys of youth, Arashiyama-san.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.460
Yes indeed!

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:46.870
Quit it.

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:50.400
It doesn't have to be at a screening. Why not a regular movie?

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:52.980
Just play it cool and ask him if he wants to go catch a flick or something.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.650
Yeah, go see something more "suitable".

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.130
The movie itself is irrelevant.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:00.240
Since the screening's at a specific date and time, I've got a better chance of success!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.410
Makes sense.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:05.860
Saying, "let's go sometime" is kind of vague, I suppose.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:09.750
So there's only one chance to catch the screening?

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.770
Yep. That's why I picked a less popular movie that wouldn't be hard to win tickets for!

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:17.610
Aww, <i>I</i>  wanna see it, though!

00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:21.820
It's hard to turn down a rare event like a screening, too.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.270
Pretty clever, Tatsuno-san.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.390
Excuse me girls...

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:26.890
You're not eating in the middle of art class, are you?

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:30.710
Care for a handful, Sensei?

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.400
Hey! That's no fair!

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:42.310
I'm checking everyone's progress, Arashiyama, so show me what you've got.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:44.240
You got it, chief.

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.050
Hey, this is pretty good!

00:03:48.050 --> 00:03:49.330
Isn't it?

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:55.060
A bit abstract, but there's a real sense of life in this horse dashing across the plains.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:57.920
It's supposed to be a sleeping dog, though...

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:00.650
That's a dog?

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:02.170
Yes, sir.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.500
Okay, next... Ebisu!

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.170
What, no follow-up?

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:09.390
Follow me!

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.370
Today's the day!

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:24.490
When Sanada comes today, I'll invite him!

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:27.570
Ugh, so hot...

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.440
What's with that slovenly appearance!?

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.280
And you call yourself a maid!?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.950
I'm ashamed to let you out in public!

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:37.820
Where the heck did that come from!?

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:41.830
The sky's the limit.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:44.380
Yeah, but it's too hot in this outfit.

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:48.210
Sew me a summer uniform, granny.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:54.640
Well, I could probably throw one together in a day or so.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:57.130
Okay... Tomorrow, the day after...

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.580
So you could do three outfits in three days!

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:02.570
If she worked three days straight, her little old heart would give out!

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:03.850
The hell it would!

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:09.720
Gotcha!

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.080
Damn, I must be in a slump.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.910
I'm getting sucked into Arashiyama-san's giddy "tee-hee" pace.

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.610
There's only 3 days left!

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.960
Today. I have to do it today.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:24.590
I have to invite Sanada-kun today, or else...

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:27.510
Hey! How's that romantic invite going?

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.130
I'm gonna do it right now, just watch.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:31.310
Woo-hoo!

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:35.800
Knowing you, I'm sure you're up to something here.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.590
I bet you'd go right up to your crush and say...

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:40.110
Heya! How's about we see a movie?

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.520
...or something, I'm sure.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:45.390
Here goes. I got it this time!

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.500
Hey, Sanada-kun...

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.650
Huh?

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:58.750
Movie...

00:05:58.750 --> 00:05:59.780
Hmm?

00:05:59.780 --> 00:06:03.030
Umm... movie...

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:05.110
Mov... movi...

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:08.130
You'd better get your butt <i>movie-ing</i> and finish cleaning up.

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:09.970
Swing and a miss!

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:20.840
Sanada's leaving, you know.

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:24.520
If you run, you can still catch him.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:28.350
Would-you-like-to-see-a-movie?

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:34.400
Why can't I say a simple 8-syllable sentence?

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:36.050
Want me to ask him for you?

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:41.900
No... I'll go.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.840
How could I have felt relieved at the idea of an indirect invite?

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:51.930
A measly 5 or 6 staircases...

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.700
...can be cleared in no time!

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:58.560
Ack! It's Kameda, the western history teacher!

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:13.270
Lu-THERRR!

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:15.080
Of all the people...

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:20.000
CZARRR!

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:25.430
Kameda, the history teacher who is said to drone on for eons once he begins a lecture.

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.350
Better known as Kameda the soft-shelled turtle!

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.870
W-Why you...

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:36.370
Arashiyama-san would probably just try to laugh her way out of a tongue lashing...

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:38.400
What would she say at a time like this?

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:41.310
How would she get herself out of it?

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:45.590
No! No, no, no!

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.790
What would <i>I</i>  do?

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.210
What would I do?

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:00.020
I'm terribly sorry, Kameda-sensei.

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:04.030
I slipped on my way down, but I'm okay.

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:11.430
A-All right then. Just be careful next time.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:15.400
Yes, sir. Excuse me.

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:24.800
Hm? Weren't you supposed to go see a movie with the fishmonger's kid?

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:30.690
I decided it'd be better to let life work for me instead of me working for it.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:34.110
That's how I choose to wield my feminine charm.

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.860
Huh? What the heck are you talking about?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.620
Oh, I see what you're up to.

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:45.360
Well, I guess I'll throw you a bone.

00:08:49.980 --> 00:08:51.630
Umm, what about the café?

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:54.170
Gramma's gonna go hit the slots.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:56.420
I’ll let the maids hold the fort today.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:00.520
In order to have sweet rice-cakes,

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:03.900
one must first make the effort to build a shelf to keep them.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:08.750
Welcome!

00:09:08.750 --> 00:09:10.370
But once in a while,

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:14.600
Yay, free movie passes! Woo-hoo!

00:09:14.600 --> 00:09:16.270
without lifting a finger,

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:19.870
there are those who's luck grants them both.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:23.870
People's true nature are reflected in their sneezes.

00:09:26.110 --> 00:09:31.210
Detectives are valued for their keen observation and their investigative instinct.

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:34.020
The job of a Japanese detective

00:09:34.020 --> 00:09:39.440
is to investigate his target's actions and secrets from the shadows.

00:09:39.440 --> 00:09:42.960
Only the most brilliant of men can perform such a task.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:46.080
I'll follow you around and observe you!

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.950
Sure you will, Detective Yukikonan.

00:09:48.950 --> 00:09:51.580
Go on and expose all my dirty little secrets.

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:52.970
AYE-AYE SIR!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:06.000
I've got no boobs or hips.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:08.360
That's your secret!

00:10:08.360 --> 00:10:11.990
You've got quite an eye for detail.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:16.110
Pillbugs are edible but they taste terrible.

00:10:16.770 --> 00:10:19.140
Get 'em! Blazing Fireball Burst!

00:10:19.940 --> 00:10:22.020
I repel it with my Mirror Shield!

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:25.640
4 life points.

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.020
Zombie Detective is defeated!

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:34.920
But when Zombie Detective dies, he can take a lower-level enemy monster with him!

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:39.660
Crud! Faerie Warrior defeated!

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.410
Next, I attack you directly!

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.650
I guard with Turtle Knight!

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:45.950
It's useless!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:50.580
My weapon is a spear-type, so I can slip past a single monster's guard!

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:55.870
Aw, man...

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:59.380
Zero life points remaining. I'm dead.

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.390
Argh, you win.

00:11:01.390 --> 00:11:02.780
You're good, Takeru!

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:04.120
You're invincible!

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:07.140
Your cards are lame, but you're still tough!

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:09.870
I bet you could take on Yamamoto from class 4!

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.650
Let's go duel during lunchtime.

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:13.650
Excuse me, boys!

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:16.460
Do you think it's okay to bring that stuff to school?

00:11:16.460 --> 00:11:17.530
Yeah!

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:19.270
Shut up, Rock Lobster!

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:20.950
Rock Lobster carpaccio!

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:23.750
I'll mention this at next week's assembly.

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.450
Let's go, Ebi-chan.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.450
You're such a nag, Rock Lobster!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:30.710
Girls are so obnoxious.

00:11:31.560 --> 00:11:32.710
Okay, class.

00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:40.720
Does anyone understand what Hans was thinking here when he suddenly ran down the stairs?

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.470
Anyone know the answer?

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:51.980
This will be on the test.

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.480
Huh?

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:57.230
Whaaaa?

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:01.480
No way.

00:12:01.480 --> 00:12:03.570
She won't actually show up.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.070
There's no way she'd come!

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.910
Oh, sorry. Bathroom's free.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.420
It's okay, that's not what I was waiting for.

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:16.420
Pardon me!

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:20.290
I-Isesaki-san...

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.550
Good afternoon!

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:24.210
Well, well, well... Hi there!

00:12:24.210 --> 00:12:26.050
So you were waiting for your little friend, huh?

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:29.560
I wasn't waiting, and she's not my friend!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:33.560
Dried bonito is the hardest food known to man.

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:37.240
I never thought she'd actually come...

00:12:37.240 --> 00:12:39.570
So why'd you come over, Isesaki-san?

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:42.570
To hang out, remember?

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:44.110
O-Oh yeah.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:44.730
Takeru!

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:45.570
Takeru!

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:48.310
Wait just a sec...

00:12:50.140 --> 00:12:51.080
What is it?

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.970
Here's a little extra for your war chest!

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:56.960
Awesome!

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:02.380
Hey, this ain't for personal use.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:03.800
Okay, gotcha.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:08.080
You bagged a real cutie! Go get 'er, tiger!

00:13:08.080 --> 00:13:09.390
Get what?

00:13:09.940 --> 00:13:13.390
Tears aren't for show.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:18.900
Well, she gave me some money, so you wanna go somewhere?

00:13:18.900 --> 00:13:19.900
Sure.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:37.290
If the guys happen to see me with a girl, I'm done for!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:43.150
Takeru, you were with a girl, <i>Isesaki</i> of all people last Sunday, correct?

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:43.860
Yes.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:48.070
The very same Isesaki who threatened to tell on us at the assembly!

00:13:48.070 --> 00:13:50.400
I plead guilty.

00:13:50.400 --> 00:13:51.180
Takeru-kun!

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:53.310
Huh?

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.780
This is boring! Say something already!

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:57.940
Uh, well...

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.980
Hey, how come you're using my first name?

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.050
You always just call me Arashiyama-kun.

00:14:03.050 --> 00:14:05.930
Huh? I can call you whatever I want.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:08.830
You call me by my first name too, Takeru-kun.

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:09.450
What!?

00:14:10.180 --> 00:14:13.990
Oh yeah, what was your first name anyway?

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:21.390
S-Sorry! I just forgot, that's all!

00:14:21.390 --> 00:14:22.650
I'm trying to remember...

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:25.000
Gimme a hint!

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:25.710
Eri...

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:26.720
Huh?

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:28.340
ERI!

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:32.350
My bark goes "arf arf", not "woof".

00:14:33.970 --> 00:14:35.060
E...

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.110
E?

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:37.570
E-E...

00:14:38.110 --> 00:14:38.940
E?

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.420
Eeeh forget it, I can't do it!

00:14:41.420 --> 00:14:44.620
It's embarrassing enough to say the name of a girl comic book character!

00:14:44.620 --> 00:14:46.190
No way!

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:49.140
Can I please just call you Ebi-chan?

00:14:49.140 --> 00:14:51.200
All the girls call you that.

00:14:52.450 --> 00:14:54.080
Fine, whatever.

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:59.580
Hey, you up for ice cream?

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:02.420
N-Nah, I'm fine. It's kinda cold out.

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.920
Well I want some, so buy it!

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.800
And don't act like such a little boy!

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.550
You're just being selfish!

00:15:10.980 --> 00:15:12.500
What flavor do you want?

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:13.180
Vanilla.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:16.850
They're out.

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:18.740
What else do they have then?

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:21.720
Pretty much everything but vanilla.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:23.610
Okay then, I'll take strawberry.

00:15:25.190 --> 00:15:27.250
Sorry, they're out of that too.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.950
And I kind of feel like I'm hypothermic.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:32.570
Okay, I'll have the same as you.

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.420
Cool, you picked chocolate melon!　

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.470
T-Thanks.

00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:41.790
It was just at the top of the pile.

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:43.870
Thanks!

00:15:45.080 --> 00:15:46.130
Hey, Takeru!

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.530
What's up? On a date?

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:52.220
Hey, hey, hey, not bad!

00:15:52.220 --> 00:15:54.590
No, that's not it.

00:15:54.590 --> 00:15:55.290
Umm...

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.240
Oh, right.

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:59.330
She's a friend of my sister.

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.600
Hey.

00:16:01.000 --> 00:16:02.690
Good afternoon.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:04.560
Hey, she's pretty cute!

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.030
Good luck, munchkin!

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:08.440
With what?

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:12.200
Sorry to bother you. Later!

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:14.180
She sure is pretty.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:15.760
Y-Yeah...

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:19.200
I thought the guys had found me.

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.780
The market's encounter rate is way too high!

00:16:22.780 --> 00:16:24.710
There's gotta be some place I can hide.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:26.380
Hey, Isesaki-san.

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:31.720
E-Ebi-chan, would you...

00:16:36.180 --> 00:16:38.870
You're coming with me to my regular joint.

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.560
Oh boy, where? I wanna see!

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:44.940
So she hits me if I say a banned word?

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:47.560
Would this count as censorship?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:55.910
Come on in!

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.490
Good afternoon!

00:16:57.490 --> 00:16:59.990
Oh, are you on a date, Takeru-kun?

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:03.500
And I guess you could call this a false accusation.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:06.710
Wow!

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:08.820
I've never been anywhere like this before!

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:12.920
I've always wanted to visit a candy store!

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:15.960
Oh, I've seen these.

00:17:15.960 --> 00:17:17.930
These are those cards you boys collect.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:18.860
Yeah.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.290
I'll take this, please.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:23.730
Sure, 1.5 million yen.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.630
But I'll cut you a deal at 150.

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:29.520
Umm, thank you very much.

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:33.740
Aww, lame. It's a duplicate.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.060
You gonna buy some cards?

00:17:35.060 --> 00:17:36.120
Just one pack.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:40.200
This is bad!

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:43.790
He still hadn't spent this month's allowance?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:46.380
I've got nowhere to run! No good excuses!

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:49.110
My grade school life is over!

00:17:49.610 --> 00:17:50.920
Oh, it's them...

00:17:52.960 --> 00:17:56.320
Takeru-kun. Go hide in the VIP room.

00:17:56.320 --> 00:17:57.050
You sure?

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.520
Hey granny, you seen Takeru?

00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:06.780
Uh-oh!

00:18:08.690 --> 00:18:11.570
We went to his house, but he wasn't home.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:15.070
I think Takeru-kun might have gone to the world of adulthood.

00:18:15.070 --> 00:18:16.970
Huh? Where?

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:21.060
Let's go check out the shrine.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:28.130
Whew! That was just like a clichéd chase scene!

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:31.000
Like they say, if you keep looking, you'll find a way.

00:18:31.380 --> 00:18:34.500
Takeru-kun. This is for you.

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:35.840
Huh? You sure?

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:36.630
Yep.

00:18:38.770 --> 00:18:39.610
Open it up!

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:40.370
Okay.

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:46.900
H-Hey, you're a little close!

00:18:46.900 --> 00:18:48.450
Did you get any strong ones?

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.400
Nothing but really weird ones, actually.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.820
Well, are these strong?

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:56.320
Yeah, if you know how to use them.

00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:59.540
Makki wanted this one,

00:18:59.540 --> 00:19:01.320
and I could trade this one to Kabaya.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:02.570
Hey, Takeru-kun.

00:19:02.990 --> 00:19:04.940
You better take good care of those.

00:19:04.940 --> 00:19:06.050
Y-Yeah, sure.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:07.830
Don't even think about trading them.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:08.580
Okay.

00:19:14.800 --> 00:19:16.840
She's totally different outside of school.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:18.400
What?

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:21.480
I won't... I mean, I ain't gonna use these.

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:23.850
How come? Aren't they real strong?

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:27.060
If I put them in my deck, I'll forget which ones are yours.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:32.810
You can do it, Takeru-kun!

00:19:33.430 --> 00:19:34.810
There, just hold onto me!

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.590
Okay, I'll let go now.

00:19:39.590 --> 00:19:41.450
Wait! Don't let go yet!

00:19:41.450 --> 00:19:46.190
Youngsters these days have no shame, flirting in broad daylight.

00:19:46.190 --> 00:19:50.550
Well, I like her. She remembers her manners.

00:19:50.550 --> 00:19:52.830
What? I didn't say I was referring to her<i>.</i>

00:19:52.830 --> 00:19:56.210
Go tell them lunch is ready, would you?

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.440
Mkay.

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.840
By the way, where's my lunch?

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.940
You can all eat together.

00:20:03.940 --> 00:20:06.350
You get along great with grade-schoolers.

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:08.140
What's that supposed to mean?

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:12.650
But I decided to dine in their company.

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:13.750
Lunch is rea... dy.

00:20:17.790 --> 00:20:19.170
Hey, Takeru!

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.120
Hey, good morning.

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:22.450
Were the heck were you yesterday?

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:25.280
Umm, just visiting a relative’s place.

00:20:26.780 --> 00:20:28.380
Hey Makita, check this out!

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:30.210
Huh, check what out?

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:32.240
Whoa, tubular!

00:20:36.700 --> 00:20:38.830
Good morning, Ebi-chan.

00:20:45.130 --> 00:20:47.680
Don't you dare call me that.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:52.370
Huh?

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:55.920
Did I...

00:20:55.920 --> 00:20:58.230
I mean, what'd I do?

00:20:58.230 --> 00:21:00.650
Cold, cold, cold!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:03.990
Beep!

00:21:05.570 --> 00:21:07.580
Sorry, sorry. Were you watching that?

00:21:08.250 --> 00:21:09.600
Look, it's not over yet.

00:21:09.600 --> 00:21:12.090
I wanted to see the transformation scene!

00:21:12.090 --> 00:21:14.360
They do the same thing every week, though.

00:21:14.360 --> 00:21:17.920
Women are such mysterious creatures.

00:21:21.190 --> 00:21:22.710
Oh man! Takeru, that was hilarious!

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:27.630
Oh, m’god I gotta write that down!

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:33.220
Oh, Takeru!

00:23:06.230 --> 00:23:10.230
It makes me sick when people use two 50 yen coins.

00:23:10.230 --> 00:23:16.990
A Japanese detective's job is to expose crimes committed by the citizens,

00:23:16.990 --> 00:23:22.000
but it’s the police who determine and execute their punishment.

00:23:22.370 --> 00:23:25.400
Okay, have you dug up any dirt on me?

00:23:25.400 --> 00:23:28.010
Yeah, I sure did.

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:29.500
Ta-daa!

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:33.500
W-Where the heck did you find that!?

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:36.050
Everything you don't want the world to see, is written right here.

00:23:38.010 --> 00:23:41.010
You win, you win! Great work, detective!

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:44.730
You know that old myth about Pandora's Box?

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:47.050
Yeah, you're not supposed to open it, right?

00:23:47.050 --> 00:23:49.800
If you do, all kinds of bad stuff comes flying out.

00:23:49.800 --> 00:23:52.440
But the last thing to fly out was hope!

00:23:52.440 --> 00:23:55.130
But hope was just a ruse!

00:23:55.130 --> 00:23:57.170
If it weren't for hope, we could just accept giving up.

00:23:57.170 --> 00:24:00.580
When the bonus round comes, I think, "I can win it back!" and keep wasting my money!

00:24:00.580 --> 00:24:03.120
Granny, did you get cleaned out at the slots?

00:24:07.270 --> 00:24:10.870
Yep, it goes round 'n round.
